## Getting in
[[ if and (eq .Edge "gateway") .InfraredHost ]]
Infrared answers at **https://[[ .InfraredHost ]]**, through Cloudflare's
proxy.[[ if .PlatformDomain ]] Zones answer at `https://<zone>.[[ .PlatformDomain ]]`.[[ end ]]
Everything else is reached by port-forward.
[[- else ]]
Everything is reached by port-forward; nothing is exposed.
[[- end ]]

```bash
# Infrared
kubectl -n [[ .InfraredNamespace ]] port-forward svc/infrared 8080:80        # http://localhost:8080

# Argo CD (user admin)
kubectl -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -o jsonpath='{.data.password}' | base64 -d; echo
kubectl -n argocd port-forward svc/argocd-server 8081:80                     # http://localhost:8081
[[ if not (contains " victoria-metrics-k8s-stack " $disabled) ]]
# Grafana (user admin)
kubectl -n monitoring get secret victoria-metrics-k8s-stack-grafana -o jsonpath='{.data.admin-password}' | base64 -d; echo
kubectl -n monitoring port-forward svc/victoria-metrics-k8s-stack-grafana 3000:80
[[ end ]][[ if not (contains " infisical " $disabled) ]]
# Infisical
kubectl -n infisical port-forward svc/infisical-infisical-standalone-infisical 8082:8080
[[ end ]]```

## Products

A product's gitops lives in **`products/<product>/`**:

```
products/<product>/
  build/image.yaml         the kpack Image that builds it (namespace builds)
  zones/<zone>/values.yaml one directory per zone: its chart values and image pin
```
[[ if .BuildRegistry ]]
`build/image.yaml` is a kpack `Image` in namespace `builds` with
`serviceAccountName: builder`, builder ClusterBuilder `infrared-builder` and
tag `[[ .BuildRegistry ]]/<product>`; see `components/builds/README.md`. The
registry repository `[[ .BuildRegistry ]]/<product>` must exist first (ECR
does not create repositories on push).
[[ else ]]
Builds are off on this cluster (no build registry), so there is nothing to
build `build/image.yaml` yet; see `components/builds/README.md`.
[[ end ]]
Add the product's Applications next to Infrared's, in
`registry/clusters/[[ .ClusterName ]]/components/`, with file names starting
**`product-<product>-`** (e.g. `product-shop-build.yaml`,
`product-shop-rc.yaml`), in an AppProject `products` that allows only the org's
repos and the product's namespaces. The root Application syncs
them like any other.

Infrared re-renders its template into this repo when it upgrades it. That
hydration writes only the files the template renders: it never deletes or
overwrites a file it does not render, so `product-*` Applications are safe,
and it never touches `products/` or `registry/clusters/[[ .ClusterName ]]/values/`.

## Configuring Infrared

Set the Infrared chart's values in
**`registry/clusters/[[ .ClusterName ]]/values/infrared.yaml`**, in a pull
request. The `infrared` Application reads it from this repo (its second
source) and works without it. Infrared never writes that file, so it survives
template upgrades, while `components/infrared.yaml` is re-rendered by each
upgrade: change that one only for the chart version. The values
`components/infrared.yaml` sets itself (cluster name, template version, pull
secret, existing Secrets, build registry) win over the file. For example, an
extension in the Infrared UI (see the chart's README, "Extensions"):

```yaml
ui:
  extensions:
    - id: wiki
      title: Wiki
      icon: book
      upstream: wiki.wiki.svc.cluster.local:8080
  extensionsProxySecret:
    existingSecret: infrared-ext-proxy
```

## Upgrading Infrared

Change the chart's `targetRevision` (the first source) in
`registry/clusters/[[ .ClusterName ]]/components/infrared.yaml` to the new
chart version, in a pull request. Do not run `helm upgrade`: Argo CD owns the
release now and would revert it.

## Secrets

Nothing secret is in this repo. The Secrets Infrared needs
(`infrared-setup`, `infrared-session`, `infrared-mcp-token`, `infrared-mcp-access`,
`infrared-api-tokens` in `[[ .InfraredNamespace ]]`) were created by the first
`helm install`, and the `infrared` Application tells the chart they exist.
[[- if not (contains " infisical " $disabled) ]]
`infisical-secrets` is generated once, on the first sync, and never rotated.
[[- end ]]
